<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<!-- 2. ABSTRACT -->
<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<h1>2. Abstract</h1>
<p>
Field Service Management (FSM) is a mission-critical capability for modern facility management and maintenance companies. Traditional service organizations rely on fragmented workflows, manual spreadsheets, phone calls, and paper work orders. This results in frequent SLA breaches, lost billing hours, untracked parts inventory, lack of visibility into field technician workloads, and degraded customer satisfaction.
</p>
<p>
<strong>Project KEYSTONE</strong> is an enterprise-grade, high-throughput Field Service and Work Order Management platform engineered for <strong>Meridian Facilities Management</strong>. The platform establishes a <strong>strictly governed 7-stage state machine</strong> for work orders, automated priority-based <strong>SLA monitoring with background breach detection</strong>, transactional <strong>inventory decrementing and technician labor time tracking</strong>, <strong>Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)</strong> across 4 distinct organizational personas (Customer, Dispatcher, Technician, Manager), an interactive <strong>7-column Kanban board</strong>, an <strong>Executive KPI Analytics Dashboard</strong>, and a <strong>Customer Self-Service Portal</strong>.
</p>
<p>
Built using <strong>Spring Boot 3 (Java 21 LTS)</strong>, <strong>PostgreSQL 16</strong>, and <strong>React 19 (Vite)</strong>, the architecture incorporates stateless <strong>JWT security</strong>, 15 versioned <strong>Flyway database migrations</strong>, a comprehensive <strong>automated unit/integration test suite</strong>, and complete containerization via <strong>Docker and Docker Compose</strong> for production deployment.
</p>

<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<!-- 3. INTRODUCTION -->
<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<h1>3. Introduction</h1>

<h2>3.1 Problem Statement</h2>
<p>
Facility management enterprises manage hundreds of high-value commercial assets (HVAC chillers, emergency generators, electrical switchboards, automated access gates, plumbing grids) across distributed client campuses. Meridian Facilities Management faced major operational bottlenecks:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Unstructured Intake & Response Delays:</strong> Clients reported equipment breakdowns via ad-hoc emails or phone calls without automated ticket triage, causing missed SLAs.</li>
  <li><strong>Untracked Parts & Labor Financials:</strong> Field technicians consumed replacement parts without atomic inventory deduction, leading to inventory discrepancies and unbilled labor hours.</li>
  <li><strong>Lack of Workflow Governance:</strong> Without an enforced state machine, work orders were prematurely closed, bypass transitions occurred, and audit trails of approvals were missing.</li>
  <li><strong>Zero Executive Visibility:</strong> Management lacked live analytics on SLA compliance rates, technician utilization, and facility-specific maintenance costs.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3.2 Motivation</h2>
<p>
The motivation for Project KEYSTONE was to engineer an end-to-end digital operations platform that streamlines the lifecycle of a maintenance request from the second a customer raises a ticket, through dispatcher scheduling, technician execution, inventory consumption, and manager audit and close-out.
</p>

<h2>3.3 Objectives</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Strict State Machine Governance:</strong> Enforce a deterministic lifecycle (<code>NEW</code> ➔ <code>ASSIGNED</code> ➔ <code>IN_PROGRESS</code> ➔ <code>ON_HOLD</code> ➔ <code>COMPLETED</code> ➔ <code>CLOSED</code>) with append-only audit logging.</li>
  <li><strong>Automated Priority-Based SLA Engine:</strong> Dynamically compute SLA deadlines by ticket priority (Critical: 2h, High: 4h, Medium: 8h/24h, Low: 48h) with background breach alerts.</li>
  <li><strong>Transactional Inventory & Labor Integrity:</strong> Atomically deduct inventory stock with non-negative invariants and log technician labor hours for real-time gross margin analytics.</li>
  <li><strong>Persona-Tailored Workspaces:</strong> Deliver purpose-built interfaces for 4 roles: Manager, Dispatcher, Technician, and Customer.</li>
  <li><strong>Cloud-Native Production Readiness:</strong> Containerize using multi-stage Docker builds and deliver interactive OpenAPI 3.0 (Swagger UI) documentation.</li>
</ul>

<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<!-- 4. PROJECT OVERVIEW -->
<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<h1>4. Project Overview</h1>
<p>
Project KEYSTONE links all four operational stakeholders in an integrated digital ecosystem:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Customer Self-Service Portal (<code>/portal</code>):</strong> Allows commercial clients to submit urgent service requests and follow real-time progress timelines from Submission to Completion.</li>
  <li><strong>Dispatcher Operations Hub (<code>/work-orders</code>):</strong> Provides an interactive 7-column Kanban board, live filtering, and 1-click technician assignment.</li>
  <li><strong>Technician Field Workbench (<code>/technicians</code>):</strong> Mobile-optimized view for field engineers to start jobs, record consumed parts, log labor minutes, and mark completion.</li>
  <li><strong>Executive Management Dashboard (<code>/dashboard</code>):</strong> Delivers live executive KPI metrics including overall SLA compliance (%), active jobs, parts/labor expenditures, and site workload distributions.</li>
</ul>

