    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>POST</code></td>
      <td><code>/api/work-orders/{id}/status</code></td>
      <td>Technician, Manager</td>
      <td>Transitions status according to the governed state machine</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>POST</code></td>
      <td><code>/api/work-orders/{id}/parts</code></td>
      <td>Technician, Dispatcher</td>
      <td>Atomically decrements parts inventory and logs part usage</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>POST</code></td>
      <td><code>/api/work-orders/{id}/time</code></td>
      <td>Technician</td>
      <td>Logs technician labor minutes and technical notes</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>GET</code></td>
      <td><code>/api/reports/summary</code></td>
      <td>Dispatcher, Manager</td>
      <td>Executive dashboard KPI summary, SLA compliance %, workload stats</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>POST</code></td>
      <td><code>/api/customer/requests</code></td>
      <td>Customer</td>
      <td>Self-service maintenance request submission</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>GET</code></td>
      <td><code>/api/customer/requests</code></td>
      <td>Customer</td>
      <td>Retrieves live status tracking for customer's own tickets</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<!-- 11. FRONTEND ARCHITECTURE -->
<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<h1>11. Frontend Architecture</h1>
<p>
The frontend is built with <strong>React 19</strong> and <strong>Vite 8</strong>. It features:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong><code>AuthContext</code>:</strong> Manages JWT token storage in <code>localStorage</code>, automatic header injection, and session expiration handling.</li>
  <li><strong><code>apiClient.js</code>:</strong> Unified fetch client with automatic bearer token attachment, error normalization, and environment-aware backend routing (<code>VITE_API_URL</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Responsive Views:</strong> Specialized dashboard, Kanban board, technician workbench, and customer self-service views.</li>
</ul>

<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<!-- 12. MAJOR FEATURES -->
<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<h1>12. Major Features</h1>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Governed State Machine:</strong> Strict transition rules preventing state skips, backed by immutable audit history logging.</li>
  <li><strong>7-Column Visual Kanban Board:</strong> Real-time card display across <code>NEW</code>, <code>ASSIGNED</code>, <code>IN_PROGRESS</code>, <code>ON_HOLD</code>, <code>COMPLETED</code>, <code>CLOSED</code>, and <code>CANCELLED</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Automated SLA Engine:</strong> Calculates SLA deadlines based on ticket priority and runs background breach detection workers.</li>
  <li><strong>Atomic Parts Decrementing:</strong> Database transactions ensure inventory stock can never go negative.</li>
  <li><strong>Customer Self-Service Portal:</strong> Enables customers to submit tickets and view real-time visual progress timelines.</li>
  <li><strong>Executive Analytics:</strong> Real-time KPI aggregation including SLA compliance %, parts and labor costs, and facility workloads.</li>
</ol>

<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<!-- 13. IMPLEMENTATION -->
<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<h1>13. Implementation</h1>

<h3>13.1 Authentication & User Management</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Stateless JWT:</strong> JJWT generates signed tokens with user email and <code>role</code> claim.</li>
  <li><strong>BCrypt Hashing:</strong> Passwords stored as one-way salted hashes in PostgreSQL.</li>
  <li><strong>Security Filter Chain:</strong> <code>JwtAuthenticationFilter</code> intercepts incoming requests and populates Spring's <code>SecurityContextHolder</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h3>13.2 Role-Based Access Control (4 Personas)</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Role</th>
      <th>Seed Email</th>
      <th>Permissions & Accessible Views</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Manager</strong></td>
      <td><code>manager@keystone.com</code></td>
      <td>Executive KPI dashboard, SLA compliance reports, final close-out signoff, customer & site management.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Dispatcher</strong></td>
      <td><code>dispatcher@keystone.com</code></td>
      <td>Work order intake, 7-column Kanban board, technician assignment, customer & site management, cancellation.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Technician</strong></td>
      <td><code>technician@keystone.com</code></td>
      <td>Field mobile view, start/hold/complete work orders, transactional parts consumption, labor time logging.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Customer</strong></td>
      <td><code>customer@keystone.com</code></td>
      <td>Customer Self-Service Portal (<code>/portal</code>), urgent maintenance ticket creation, real-time ticket tracking.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

