<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<!-- 15. TESTING -->
<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<h1>15. Testing</h1>
<p>
Project KEYSTONE includes an automated test suite executed via Maven:
</p>
<div class="code-block">
cd KEYSTONE
./mvnw test
</div>

<h3>Verified Test Classes:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong><code>KeystoneApplicationTests</code>:</strong> Validates Spring ApplicationContext bootstrap, Flyway schema validation, and Hibernate entity mappings.</li>
  <li><strong><code>WorkOrderLifecycleTest</code>:</strong> Comprehensive lifecycle tests verifying valid state progression (<code>NEW</code> ➔ <code>ASSIGNED</code> ➔ <code>IN_PROGRESS</code> ➔ <code>COMPLETED</code> ➔ <code>CLOSED</code>), rejection of illegal transitions (409 Conflict), and unauthorized close-out attempts.</li>
  <li><strong><code>InventoryTransactionTest</code>:</strong> Validates transactional stock deduction, rejection of requests exceeding available stock, and invariant preservation.</li>
  <li><strong><code>ReportingServiceTest</code>:</strong> Verifies Executive KPI calculations, SLA compliance percentage aggregation, and technician workload rollups.</li>
  <li><strong><code>SecurityRbacTests</code>:</strong> Tests stateless JWT generation, cryptographic claim signature parsing, and rejection of malformed tokens.</li>
</ul>

<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<!-- 16. DEPLOYMENT -->
<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<h1>16. Deployment</h1>

<h3>16.1 Docker Compose Local Orchestration</h3>
<p>
The application can be started locally with a single command:
</p>
<div class="code-block">
git clone https://github.com/surajit654/Keystone.git
cd Keystone
docker-compose up --build
</div>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Frontend Web App:</strong> <code>http://localhost:3000</code></li>
  <li><strong>Backend REST API:</strong> <code>http://localhost:8080</code></li>
  <li><strong>Interactive OpenAPI Swagger UI:</strong> <code>http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html</code></li>
  <li><strong>PostgreSQL Database:</strong> <code>localhost:5432</code> (db: <code>keystone</code>, user: <code>postgres</code>, pass: <code>password</code>)</li>
</ul>

<h3>16.2 Cloud Deployment (Railway)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Backend:</strong> Deployed as a Docker / Java service with <strong>Root Directory</strong> = <code>/KEYSTONE</code> connected to Railway PostgreSQL.</li>
  <li><strong>Frontend:</strong> Deployed as a web service with <strong>Root Directory</strong> = <code>/frontend</code> and environment variable <code>VITE_API_URL</code> pointing to the backend.</li>
</ul>

<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<!-- 17. CHALLENGES & SOLUTIONS -->
<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<h1>17. Challenges & Solutions</h1>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>#</th>
      <th>Technical Challenge</th>
      <th>Engineering Solution</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>1</td>
      <td><strong>Preventing Illegal State Machine Skips</strong></td>
      <td>Implemented strict transition validation in <code>WorkOrderService</code> returning HTTP <code>409 Conflict</code> when invalid transitions are attempted.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>2</td>
      <td><strong>Preventing Inventory Stock Race Conditions</strong></td>
      <td>Applied <code>@Transactional</code> boundaries with pre-check invariants to ensure inventory stock cannot drop below zero.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>3</td>
      <td><strong>Real-Time Customer-to-Kanban Synchronization</strong></td>
      <td>Unified Customer Portal requests with the <code>WorkOrder</code> entity, generating unique tracking codes (<code>WO-YYYY-XXXX</code>) that appear instantly on the Kanban board.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>4</td>
      <td><strong>Cross-Origin Deployment Compatibility (CORS)</strong></td>
      <td>Configured <code>CorsConfig</code> with <code>allowedOriginPatterns("*")</code> and dynamic <code>VITE_API_URL</code> support for seamless multi-domain cloud hosting.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<!-- 18. LEARNING OUTCOMES -->
<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<h1>18. Learning Outcomes</h1>
<ul>
  <li>Architecting enterprise Java applications with <strong>Spring Boot 3</strong> and <strong>Java 21 LTS</strong>.</li>
  <li>Implementing stateless security and <strong>Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)</strong> using JSON Web Tokens (JWT).</li>
  <li>Managing database migrations and schema versioning using <strong>Flyway</strong> and <strong>PostgreSQL 16</strong>.</li>
  <li>Building reactive, high-performance user interfaces using <strong>React 19</strong>, <strong>Vite</strong>, and CSS design tokens.</li>
  <li>Multi-stage containerization with <strong>Docker</strong> and <strong>Docker Compose</strong> for automated cloud deployments.</li>
</ul>

<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<!-- 19. FUTURE SCOPE -->
<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<h1>19. Future Scope</h1>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Real-Time WebSockets / SSE:</strong> Push live status updates directly to Dispatcher and Technician boards without manual polling.</li>
  <li><strong>GPS & Route Optimization:</strong> Integrate map services to provide optimal routing for technicians across service sites.</li>
  <li><strong>Mobile App with Offline Support:</strong> Progressive Web App (PWA) with offline caching for field engineers working in low-connectivity areas.</li>
  <li><strong>AI Predictive Maintenance:</strong> Machine learning models to forecast equipment failures before critical breakdowns occur.</li>
</ol>

<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<!-- 20. CONCLUSION -->
<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<h1>20. Conclusion</h1>
<p>
Project KEYSTONE provides a robust, enterprise-grade Field Service and Work Order Management platform for Meridian Facilities Management. By enforcing strict state machine governance, automated SLA monitoring, transactional inventory tracking, 4-role RBAC security, and an intuitive modern UI, the platform eliminates paper work orders, streamlines dispatch operations, protects inventory margins, and empowers executive decision-making.
</p>

